==Old Norse==

===Etymology===
{{proto|Germanic|harja-|lang=non}}, whence also Gothic {{term|𐌷𐌰𐍂𐌾𐌹𐍃|sc=Goth|tr=harjis||army, host|lang=got}}, Old High German ''[[heri]]'', Old English ''[[here]]''. Relation to Sanskrit {{term|कुल|sc=Deva|tr=kula||flock, herd, family|lang=sa}} has been theorised <ref>[http://germazope.uni-trier.de/Projects/WBB/woerterbuecher/dwb/wbgui?lemmode=lemmasearch&mode=hierarchy&textsize=600&onlist=&word=Heer&lemid=GH04786&query_start=1&totalhits=0&textword=&locpattern=&textpattern=&lemmapattern=&verspattern=#GH04786L0 Heer] in [[DWB#German|DWB]]</ref>.

